sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Caller
    participant Host as Extension Host
    participant Control as Registry, Installation, and Policy
    participant Runtime as Isolated Extension Runtime
    participant Provider as Domain or Platform Provider
    participant Resource as Tenant Resource
    participant Evidence as Evidence and Usage

    Caller->>Host: Invoke extension point with tenant context
    Host->>Control: Verify package, installation, grant, policy, and budget
    Control-->>Host: Exact digest and bounded execution authority

    alt Admission denied or package suspended
        Host-->>Caller: Stable tenant-safe denial
        Host->>Evidence: Record admission decision
    else Execution admitted
        Host->>Runtime: Start bounded execution with mediated interfaces
        Runtime->>Host: Request granted provider capability
        Host->>Provider: Call with extension and tenant execution identity
        Provider->>Provider: Validate actor, grant, resource ownership, and policy

        alt Provider denies or runtime fails
            Provider-->>Host: Classified failure
            Host->>Runtime: Cancel, limit, or quarantine
            Host->>Evidence: Record denial, failure, and resource use
            Host-->>Caller: Contract-defined failure or safe omission
        else Operation permitted
            Provider->>Resource: Execute authoritative tenant operation
            Resource-->>Provider: Tenant-bound result
            Provider-->>Host: Validated response
            Host->>Runtime: Return mediated result
            Runtime-->>Host: Extension output
            Host->>Evidence: Record package, grant, outcome, health, and usage
            Host-->>Caller: Validated extension-point response
        end
    end
